package standard.io.log

import standard.io.Async

/// A backend that consumes `LogRecord` values. Implementors choose how (and
/// where) records are rendered and written: stderr, a file, an in-memory
/// buffer, etc.
///
/// `emit` returns `Async<Unit, Never>` — sink implementations must absorb
/// their own I/O errors (logging is best-effort and must not pollute the
/// caller's error channel). The built-in sinks fall back to writing a one-line
/// diagnostic to stderr when their underlying stream fails.
///
/// Sinks that buffer (Console, File) are constructed as `Resource<Sink, E>`
/// values; the Resource's release runs a final flush before closing. Callers
/// `use` the resource at top-level main, so flushing on shutdown (success or
/// panic) is automatic and the trait itself has no `flush` method.
public interface LogSink =
    /// Render `event` and write it. Called once per emitted log event.
    function emit(self: Self, event: LogRecord): Async<Unit, Never>
